<code>assert e != null => !this.containsKey(key) && !this.containsValue(e.value);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert e != null => !this.containsKey(key) && !this.containsValue(e.value);</code>

This assert statement captures the specification that if the key was previously in the map (i.e., `e != null`), then after the removal operation, the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsKey(key)`) and the value associated with the key is also no longer present in the map (`!this.containsValue(e.value)`).
